-- @ends-because above a rule L4 finds no way back to itself from: the mark
-- draws a warning that it sees nothing to explain, beside the note every mark
-- leaves. Beside it, the same mark above a rule that does use itself again,
-- which draws no such warning. Described in
-- doc/reference/regulative/rules-that-start-themselves-again.md.

-- Warns: nothing for the mark to explain.
@ends-because it is only arithmetic
GIVEN rent IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`late fee` rent MEANS rent TIMES 0.05

-- No such warning: the rule uses itself again.
@ends-because each step moves one day nearer the end date
GIVEN d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`days left` d MEANS
    IF d AT MOST 0 THEN 0 ELSE `days left` (d MINUS 1)
